  "body": "What happens: `cargo test -p xtask` fails on main c0c92ee86: `gate_maps_tests::no_gate_map_names_a_moved_module_as_app` - \"Gate maps naming moved modules as app::<module>: [lathe_post_thread_dips: app::post]\" (crates/app/tests/lathe_post_thread_dips.rs:15-17).\n\nCause: PR #2115 was stacked on #468 (branch issue/419-thread-dips, head d3bb673d at the time). Merging #2115 (ea64d16b6, M5's merge batch 2026-11-18) also brought #468's commits up to d3bb673d onto main. The new test file's Gate map still says `app::post`, which moved to the post crate. In addition, #468's later commits are NOT on main: 98673578c, c4c7ede52, 83d89b466, 8f99bcb4c (`fix(threading): align dip motion readers and pin controls`), so main has the chip-break-dips feature without its last review fixes.\n\nFix plan (M5): (1) refresh #468 against main now (merge main into its branch, keep its fixes), fix the Gate map line there, re-gate and merge it next; (2) if that takes long, a one-line Gate map fix first so main is green.\n\nDone means: `cargo test -p xtask` green on main, and #468's remaining commits (incl. 8f99bcb4c) on main.\n",
